    "name": "ScreenSanctionsWatchlist",
    "description": "Screens applicant name (for retail) or both personal name and business entity name (for business applications) against Office of Foreign Assets Control (OFAC) Specially Designated Nationals (SDN) list and consolidated sanctions lists (sectoral sanctions, foreign sanctions evaders, etc.) to ensure institution does not provide financial services to prohibited persons per Treasury Department regulations. Uses fuzzy name-matching algorithms including Levenshtein edit distance (character-level differences) and Soundex/Metaphone phonetic similarity to account for spelling variations, transliteration from non-Latin characters, aliases, middle name inclusion/omission, and data entry errors. Returns match result with confidence score 0-100: 'clear' (<75 indicating no significant match), 'potential_match' (75-95 requiring human AML analyst adjudication for false positive determination), 'confirmed_match' (>95 with corroborating attributes like DOB/address match causing immediate automatic decline without adverse action notice per OFAC regulations). Potential matches route to Sanctions Review Queue where trained compliance analysts examine applicant details vs. sanctioned party record and document determination as 'False Positive - Proceed' or 'True Positive - Reject'. Confirmed matches trigger blocked assets reporting to OFAC if any funds transfer involved (e.g., secured card deposit payment).",
